            <ArticleTitle>Anterior myocardial infarction patterns in the mitral valve prolapse-systolic click sydrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>719-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two young women with the mitral valve prolapse-systolic click (MVP-SC) syndrome had electrocardiographic and vectorcardiographic evidence of transmural anterior myocardial infarction in the absence of clinical and arteriographic evidence of coronary disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
